            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.8 (build 715)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Which door they came through.</b> The arrow beside <b>Copy</b> on a personal link copies it tagged for Slack, a text message or a chat, and the Email draft tags itself. Activity then reads &#8220;via Slack&#8221; on each open.</li>
<li><b>More of what they watched.</b> Each clip&#8217;s line now says how much of the viewing was in a compare or in full screen, and a clip that was only seen as the B side of a compare is credited for it. Reaching the end only counts with the tab in front.</li>
<li><b>Invited, never opened.</b> If the studio watcher keeps your reviews, its daily record now tells the owners &#8212; once per person, a day after their link was made &#8212; who hasn&#8217;t opened theirs.</li>
<li><b>Export Activity as PDF</b>, beside CSV, in Past Reviews.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
