            <sparkle:version>711</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.8</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.8 (build 711)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>See what each person watched.</b> Under each personal link in Activity: how long each clip actually played in front of them, how many times through, whether they reached the end, and a heat strip showing where in the clip the viewing time went &#8212; the shot someone watched six times stands out. Playback with the tab hidden is counted apart. The page sends this encrypted for your Mac alone, so neither the relay nor anyone else in the review can read it; it arrives live while you host, and waits for you when you don&#8217;t. It is kept with the review in Past Reviews, and the CSV export gains a row per person and clip. Only personal links report; the ordinary link logs nothing.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
